# 1️⃣ What is a Transaction?

A **Transaction** is a sequence of database operations treated as a **single logical unit of work**.

Example:

```sql id="1lmbph"
BEGIN TRANSACTION

Debit ₹1000 from Account A

Credit ₹1000 to Account B

COMMIT
```

If any step fails:

```sql id="sdzqvj"
ROLLBACK
```

---

# 2️⃣ Transaction States

```text id="njahxg"
Active
   ↓
Partially Committed
   ↓
Committed
```

If an error occurs:

```text id="3y1t4y"
Active
   ↓
Failed
   ↓
Aborted
```

