# 3️⃣ ACID Properties

## A — Atomicity

"All or Nothing."

Either the entire transaction completes or none of it does.

Example:

Bank transfer.

---

## C — Consistency

A transaction must move the database from one **valid state** to another.

Constraints must always hold.

---

## I — Isolation

Concurrent transactions should not interfere with each other.

Users should behave as if transactions execute one after another.

---

## D — Durability

Once committed, changes are **permanent**, even after a power failure.

📌 **GATE Tip:** ACID properties are among the most frequently asked DBMS concepts.

